  "character_tex": "$b_{(\\lambda;\\,j)}$ are the branching functions of $SO(5)_2$ into the principal $SU(2)_{20}$, $\\chi^{SO(5)_2}_{\\lambda}(q, z^{2\\rho^\\vee}) = \\sum_j b_{(\\lambda;\\,j)}(q)\\,\\chi^{SU(2)_{20}}_j(q,z)$, for $\\lambda\\in\\{\\mathbf{1},\\mathbf{5},\\mathbf{10},\\mathbf{14}\\}$ with integer $j$ and $\\lambda\\in\\{\\mathbf{4},\\mathbf{16}\\}$ with half-integer $j$; $(\\lambda;\\,j)\\sim(J\\lambda;\\,10-j)$ with $J$ exchanging $\\mathbf{1}\\leftrightarrow\\mathbf{14}$, $\\mathbf{4}\\leftrightarrow\\mathbf{16}$. Blocks: $\\chi_{(\\lambda;\\,j)} = b_{(\\lambda;\\,j)}$, and $\\chi^{\\pm}_{(\\lambda;\\,5)} = \\tfrac12(b_{(\\lambda;\\,5)}\\pm\\delta_\\lambda)$ at the fixed points with Lee–Yang characters $\\delta_{\\mathbf{5}} = q^{-1/60}G(q)$, $\\delta_{\\mathbf{10}} = q^{11/60}H(q)$ (Rogers–Ramanujan functions $G$, $H$).",
  "description": "Weyl–Kac characters of $SO(5)_2$ in the principal grading are decomposed exactly into $SU(2)_{20}$ characters; $-1$ in the principal $SU(2)$ is the non-trivial centre element of $Spin(5)$, so spinors carry half-integer $j$ and field identification combines the $SO(5)_2$ simple current with $j\\to10-j$. Through the conformal embedding $SO(5)_2\\subset SU(5)_1$ (verified on the characters) the fixed points $(\\mathbf{5};5)$ and $(\\mathbf{10};5)$ have the branching functions of $SU(5)_1/SU(2)_{20}$, and they are resolved with the same Lee–Yang twining characters, checked against the resolved (Schellekens–Yankielowicz 1990) $S$-matrix and its fusion rules. Diagonal invariant.",
